    "format": "csv",
    "shard_size_mb": 8192,
    "why_this_scale": "JOB 1 measured finance frac = 0.05424*pi, so pi=0.05 gives ~0.26% of edges anomalous. At 1e7 edges that is ~26k anomalous edges: above the ~20k target for training while keeping the base rate at its honest intrinsic value (~0.26%, NOT the ~30% the elasticity bug used to produce). 1e8 edges would give ~260k positives but a 6GB+ CSV that detector.py must read into pandas; 1e7 is the largest scale that trains comfortably and it already clears the positives bar.",
    "shard_note": "--shard-size 8192 forces a single edges_00000.csv because detector.py reads only the first edges*.csv shard; no data is changed by this.",
    "edge_invariance_check": "finance pi=0.05 delta=0.5 (the default) at 1e7 -> 25,780/9,983,506 = 0.2582%; JOB 1's same config at 1e8 -> 258,677/99,803,433 = 0.2592%. The anomaly fraction is edge-count-invariant to within 0.4% relative, confirming the elasticity fix."
  },
